WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.480
CHEERFUL SKEWERS

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:03.480
Kisaragi! Get the order for table two, please!

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.480
Got it, Mr. Kanemoto!

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:07.980
I recommend the garland chrysanthemum.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:10.940
<i>It's been one week since I started working.</i>

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>I'm finally starting to get used to it.</i>

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:16.490
The assorted kabob plate, right?

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.490
I'll be right back with it.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:53.380
EPISODE 09
MY CONCLUSION
AFTER MUCH
CONSIDERATION

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:53.050
Joro, good job today.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.010
You, too, Tsubaki.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.970
Compared to your first day,
you've really gotten the hang of it.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:01.800
R-Really?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.520
You pick things up quickly, Joro.

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:08.690
Mr. Kanemoto said he only has to tell you
something once, and you're able to do it.

00:02:09.350 --> 00:02:10.900
That's laying it on thick.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:14.650
Joro, you should have
more confidence in yourself.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:18.400
Everyone around me
is too talented for me to think like that.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.120
In the end, I'm just a background character.

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.620
Joro.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:32.960
Mornings are so peaceful
without that ditzy bitch around.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.420
Good morning, Joro!

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.840
Joro, a proper morning greeting
is "Good morning," not "Eeegya!"

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:44.050
Wh-What are you doing here?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.310
Before the tournament,
don't you have morning practice?

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.020
Um, uh...

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:51.020
today's our day off!

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:55.730
<i>Her eyes moved once to the right
and twice to the left. I see. She's lying.</i>

00:02:55.980 --> 00:03:00.320
I-I bet you've been lonely lately, Joro,
not being able to walk to school together!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.950
It's an important tournament,
so tennis needs to be your priority.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:09.160
I know! We're going to win this year for sure
and get our good name back!

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:11.330
<i>All you've got now is a bad reputation.</i>

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:12.170
Huh?

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.630
What's that book?

00:03:14.630 --> 00:03:16.590
Um, this is...

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:18.840
n-nothing important!

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:21.260
I'm just reading it to kill time!

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:24.640
That book is all beat up.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.100
Why don't you buy a new one?

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:30.810
I-I don't need a new one!
Like I said, it's not important.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:32.060
Oh.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:35.520
Anyway, Himawari,
your birthday is coming up, huh?

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.780
I'll get you an awesome present,
believe me.

00:03:38.940 --> 00:03:40.740
Really? Yay!

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:42.700
Thank you, Joro!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.700
<i>I managed to shake her off the scent.</i>

00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:58.750
<i>She's been in a lousy mood
ever since I started working.</i>

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:04.680
Pansy, Joro's doing his best,
so I think it's a good thing.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.430
I agree, yeah.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:09.930
Yes, I agree as well.

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:12.770
But I'm not entirely convinced.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:13.850
Sheesh.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:20.900
<i>At least if Himawari were here...</i>

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:24.860
<i>Why did she have to have a club meeting
today of all days?</i>

00:04:25.110 --> 00:04:27.280
Pansy, it's okay.

00:04:27.280 --> 00:04:32.250
Joro's already said that once he reaches
his monetary goal, he'll cut back on hours.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.330
So, soon enough, Joro will come home to you.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.790
<i>Where does she think I live, anyway?</i>

00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:39.920
I know.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.510
CHEERFUL SKEWERS

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:47.550
Welcome!

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:50.470
Huh? You work here?

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.020
I didn't know.
Coincidences are scary, right? Everyone?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:56.980
H-Huh?

00:04:57.310 --> 00:05:00.440
Why am I the only one?
We were supposed to all come in!

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:04.610
Amazing!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.570
Party of five?

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:12.500
Aren't you glad we came?

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.920
Hey, cut it out!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:20.380
Thank you for coming.

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.380
If I feel like it, I'll come back sometime.

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:25.840
W-Work hard.

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:26.760
See you!

00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:27.930
Thanks, Joro!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:29.090
It was really good!

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.220
See you!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:31.760
All right!

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.770
I'll carry that, too.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:37.060
You're already carrying drinks, Joro, so I'll...

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.480
I've got it!

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.070
You focus on the cooking, Tsubaki.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.610
All right, maybe I'll have you handle that.

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.440
Yeah!

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:50.700
Ow-ow-ow.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:52.700
Don't give me "ow-ow-ow"!

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:04.340
What's the idea
of drenching a customer with beer?

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:07.590
I apologize! I'm so sorry!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.260
You think an apology will make it okay?

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.930
Go to hell!
I'm sure the only reason you're working

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:17.140
is you've got nothing better to do
and figure you'll make a little money.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:20.100
- That's not it—
- You have no clue about the real world!

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.230
- I-I'm sorry!
- Sir.

00:06:23.320 --> 00:06:27.490
We sincerely apologize
for the inconvenience this has caused.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:33.740
This is our fault, so please
let us pay for the dry cleaning.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.290
Fine. You know how to do your job, at least.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.630
<i>Really, what the hell am I doing?</i>

00:06:48.510 --> 00:06:51.090
<i>Causing problems for Tsubaki like that...</i>

00:06:51.090 --> 00:06:53.390
<i>How could I be so klutzy?</i>

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:58.350
What are you doing here?

00:06:58.770 --> 00:07:00.520
And dressed like that?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:07.110
I wanted to talk to your true self,
so I waited for you in this form.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:12.700
My true self?
Quit talking nonsense, and go home.

00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.910
How was work today?

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.370
Damn it. You heard from Tsubaki, didn't you?

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:24.880
A customer got pissed off and read me
the riot act. You got a complaint?

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:29.340
I have nothing but complaints about
a part-time job you work at for the worst reason.

00:07:29.720 --> 00:07:31.720
Why do you think I'm working in the—

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.590
To save face, that's why.

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.310
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.430
Sun-chan is aiming for Koushien.

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:43.480
Himawari is a tennis ace.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:46.480
Cosmos is the student council president.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.190
Tsubaki runs a restaurant.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:52.110
You compare yourself to everyone else
and come up short,

00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:55.410
so you wanted to solve this incident
by yourself somehow.

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:58.160
Therefore, your actions this time...

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:01.120
don't show kindness to anyone.

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.380
Self-satisfaction
masquerading as benevolence...

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:09.130
That's the emotion
I hate the most in this world.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:14.470
Screw you! Even if that's so,
you have no right to fault me for it!

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:17.390
What the hell do you want me to do?

00:08:17.850 --> 00:08:21.390
What do I have? Nothing!

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:24.520
I have nothing.

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:28.360
You have me.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:32.780
You've got me, and I love you
more than you know.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.110
That's...

00:08:34.110 --> 00:08:35.200
It's okay.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.580
It's okay, Joro.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:41.330
You're already a good person.

00:08:43.910 --> 00:08:45.000
So...

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.090
Pansy...

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.680
get lost.

00:09:03.560 --> 00:09:04.810
All right.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.750
I really am an asshole.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:29.080
<i>I couldn't break my promise,
so I came to the school library, but...</i>

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:29.590
LIBRARY

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:33.380
Hey, Pansy!
My tournament is just around the corner!

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.590
I'm going to give it all I've got!

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.300
I'm really looking forward to it.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:41.060
I'll be there to cheer you on, Himawari.

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:43.310
Thank you!

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:47.100
<i>Himawari being here
is the one saving grace.</i>

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.770
<i>Times like this, you need
someone to liven up the mood.</i>

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:54.650
Oh, that's right! Hey, Joro!
Did you finish reading that tattered book?

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:57.150
<i>Mood breaker!</i>

00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.620
N-No. Not yet.

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.950
I know! You won't finish reading it
until you buy a new one!

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.460
That's dumb!

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:11.840
It's okay, though! I'll do my best!

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:14.630
After all, what are old friends for?

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:15.920
See you guys later!

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:16.800
See you!

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.680
See you later, Himawari.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:20.260
<i>What's "okay"?</i>

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.430
Hey, Joro.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:27.100
What's up, Sun-chan?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:30.480
If you want to protect
what's important to you,

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.020
don't worry about your reputation
or being ashamed.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:35.610
There's nothing wrong with trying,
even if you expect a swing and a miss.

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.530
Um...

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.990
Well, that's all. Let's both do our best!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:49.830
You can clock out for today, Joro.

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:52.080
But the shift isn't over.

00:10:52.420 --> 00:10:57.550
If the customers see you with that long face,
the food won't taste any good.

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:00.760
Go home, get some rest,
and think about it a little.

00:11:01.300 --> 00:11:05.890
Think about why you're working
and what you want to accomplish.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:09.480
What I want to accomplish?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.900
Then, from tomorrow,
I want to work with the cheerful Joro again.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:17.650
MIZUYAMA PARK

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.860
It's just a vicious circle.

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:26.200
Excuse me. Um...

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:28.870
Can I use that?

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:34.250
Hey, meeting here like this, maybe it's fate.

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:36.090
Want to talk about it?

00:11:37.090 --> 00:11:40.300
I can't walk away when you've got
that expression on your face.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.680
I see. So you had a fight
with someone special to you.

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:50.560
Yeah. The cause was
my own inferiority complex.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:55.810
So my guess is you want
to patch things up with that person?

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.270
Well, yeah...

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:59.440
but I have no idea how to do it.

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:03.660
Maybe all you need to do
is what you think you should do.

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:09.620
When you don't know what to do,
try anything, pull levers like a madman.

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:13.580
At least, that's what I've always done.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:18.630
If you really want to protect
the person who means a lot to you,

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:21.050
you can't think about yourself getting hurt.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:25.260
The thing you should focus on the most
is that person, right?

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.770
<i>If you want to protect
what's important to you,</i>

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.390
<i>there's nothing wrong with trying,
even if you expect a swing and a miss.</i>

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:35.650
Maybe Sun-chan
was trying to tell me that, too.

00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:38.110
I see.

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:39.610
You're right!

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:43.610
I can't be afraid! I have to go all out
and try something in my own way!

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:45.820
Yep. That's the spirit.

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.450
Y-Yeah!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:50.660
Wait. I should've said before.
I didn't tell you my name.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.910
I'm Kisaragi. Amatsuyu Kisaragi.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:57.420
I'm Hazuki. Yasuo Hazuki.

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.130
Thank you!

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:01.960
You're welcome.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:09.050
What is it?
Why did you want to meet me here?

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:10.810
I'm so sorry for the other day.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:16.400
When you put a name to my true feelings,
I felt pathetic and took it out on you.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:20.190
So then I thought about it in my own way.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.110
I'm going to keep working.

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:28.030
Not to erase a debt to you,
but because I want to buy you a new book.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.040
Oh. Okay.

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:35.330
Joro.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.540
Work hard.

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:42.760
I will!

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.310
CHEERFUL SKEWERS

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.020
PAYCHECK

00:14:00.110 --> 00:14:02.730
This is the proof
that you've been working hard, Joro.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:06.530
I thought it would be better to give it
to you directly. I prepared it special like this.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.240
Thank you for all of your hard work.

00:14:10.660 --> 00:14:13.700
Maybe now you can accomplish
what you wanted to do.

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.540
Yeah, maybe I can!

00:14:16.080 --> 00:14:17.330
Good luck, Joro!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.710
Thanks! I'll be back!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:23.920
What? I'm in a hurry.

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.510
<i>Hey, where are you, Joro? I want to see you!</i>

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.760
<i>Sorry. It's kind of crowded here,
so I don't think I can get away.</i>

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:35.140
<i>Have a good practice.</i>

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.980
As I recall, it was around here.

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:44.480
USED BOOKSTORE
SHIMAKI BOOKSTORE

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:46.610
Here it is!

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:49.950
I'm sorry.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.280
A girl bought our last copy
just a few minutes ago.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:55.740
Um, do you know
of any other places that have it?

00:14:55.740 --> 00:14:57.960
- I don't know.
- Yeah, I didn't think so.

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:04.380
<i>Why is this happening?</i>

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.630
<i>What should I say to Pansy—</i>

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.630
Joro!

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.670
Geez, you're late!

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:10.090
H-Himawari?

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.340
That's right. It's me, Himawari.

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.350
Why are you here?

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:16.810
It's before a match,
so you've got practice on the weekends.

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:19.520
NATSUME SOUSEKI
HAND-WRITTEN ESSAY
KOKORO

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.520
Ta-da!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:23.480
- This is for you!
- You...

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.110
Don't tell me...

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.610
See? Now it's okay!

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:30.610
When did you start looking for that?

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.660
I-I guess since yesterday.

00:15:33.660 --> 00:15:35.160
<i>Wrong. She's lying.</i>

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.410
<i>She skipped practice
to search for it even before.</i>

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:40.410
NATSUME SOUSEKI
HAND-WRITTEN ESSAY
KOKORO

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:40.410
It was expensive, wasn't it?

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:44.130
That's all right. I had a lot of money saved up.

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:45.590
Saved up?

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:48.550
Did you use the money
you were going to buy a racket with?

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:52.890
Um, uh, but, anyway, this is for you!

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:53.970
Take it!

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:58.270
Now you'll be cheerful again!

00:15:58.270 --> 00:15:59.560
Isn't that good?

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:02.020
Shove it.

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.690
What are you doing?

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:07.480
You're right before an important match!

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:13.410
I told you to never mind me
and make tennis your first priority!

00:16:14.030 --> 00:16:15.950
You've been skipping practice, haven't you?

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:18.490
You used your money
for the new racket, didn't you?

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:22.710
B-But you were in a bind. So I...

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.330
I was in a bind?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.710
How the hell would you know that?

00:16:29.050 --> 00:16:30.210
I-I could tell!

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:34.550
I know! I definitely know!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:38.640
You lied to me, Joro!
You said that book wasn't important!

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:41.350
<i>Wait. She could tell that I was lying?</i>

00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:45.100
Since I caused you trouble,
I wanted to be the one to fix it!

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.610
So why? Why aren't you happy about it?

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:50.900
Why are you angry at me?

00:16:50.900 --> 00:16:53.740
O-Of course I'm angry!
You've got a tennis match!

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:57.240
Tennis is important to me,
but you're just as important!

00:16:57.240 --> 00:16:58.370
So...

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.830
Me? Forget me!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.500
Your dream is more important!

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.960
You've worked so hard all this time!

00:17:06.960 --> 00:17:08.670
It's an important match, right?

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.460
So why would you prioritize me over that?

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:14.720
Of course that wouldn't make me happy!

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:19.220
- I-I'm sorry.
- Himawari, sorry, I was...

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:21.680
I'm sorry!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:27.400
I'm sorry, Joro!

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.570
No, I'm sorry. That was too harsh.

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.490
No! You didn't do anything wrong!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:38.070
I'm sorry!
I just made even more trouble for you.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.740
I'm sorry!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.950
It's not trouble.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:48.290
To be honest, I'm touched
you bought the book for me.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:52.800
It makes me thankful
that we're old friends, Himawari.

00:17:53.590 --> 00:17:54.920
Really?

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:55.760
Yeah!

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:00.890
Joro!

00:18:00.890 --> 00:18:02.010
Joro! Joro!

00:18:02.010 --> 00:18:05.230
Um, thank you for helping me.

00:18:05.430 --> 00:18:06.640
Sure!

00:18:06.640 --> 00:18:09.100
NATIONAL HIGH SCHOOL
TENNIS QUALIFIER TOURNAMENT

00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:11.110
Everyone!

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:13.400
Better not lose, Himawari!

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:15.240
Try not to be too nervous.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.450
I think we've got everything
for the victory celebration.

00:18:18.450 --> 00:18:20.320
Knowing you, I'm sure you'll win.

00:18:21.660 --> 00:18:22.990
Thanks everyone!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:26.080
Hey, Joro.

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:27.080
Yeah?

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.210
Is there a girl you like right now?

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:32.800
I told you when we did the Flower Dance.

00:18:32.800 --> 00:18:33.920
There's not.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:37.680
I see. Then, that's not the same as me.

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:40.850
Isn't that different from before?

00:18:40.850 --> 00:18:43.810
Since you answered my question,
I'll give you a reward.

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:51.730
Thank you for the birthday present, Joro!

00:18:51.730 --> 00:18:53.270
I'll take good care of it!

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.690
I'll treasure it always!

00:18:55.690 --> 00:18:57.240
Well, see you guys later!

00:18:57.950 --> 00:19:00.570
This week's title
has nothing to do with anything!

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:06.830
I won't lose!

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:09.580
Cheers!

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:11.580
You did it, Himawari!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:13.630
Keep it up for the next one!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:15.050
I will! Thanks!

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.840
Himawari worked so hard for it.

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:20.550
I've got to do my best, too!

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:24.640
Waiter, can I ask you a question?

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:26.600
What is it?

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:31.020
NATSUME SOUSEKI
HAND-WRITTEN ESSAY
KOKORO

00:19:28.930 --> 00:19:31.020
I wanted to ask you what you thought.

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:33.730
You read the whole book, didn't you?

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:37.110
Well, it was interesting.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.070
Is that all?

00:19:40.400 --> 00:19:42.950
That's all... I think...

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:48.790
<i>A bookmark. This was in there?</i>

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:52.920
IF I'M EVER
IN A LOT OF TROUBLE,
WOULD YOU HELP ME?

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:54.250
<i>If I'm ever in a lot of trouble,
would you help me?</i>

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.010
If I have free time then.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.760
That's a lovely opinion.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.930
What? I have to get back to work.

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:10.850
You should be participating
in the victory party, too, Joro.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.850
I can't let you work by yourself, Tsubaki.

00:20:14.230 --> 00:20:17.110
Besides, you said you wanted
to tell me something, right?

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:21.780
By working, you've gained confidence
in yourself and have become able to act.

00:20:22.200 --> 00:20:27.330
So now, more than ever,
I'd truly like to pay you back.

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:31.160
Oh, you've already done more than enough
for me. Anymore than this would be...

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:32.000
Joro.

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:35.960
Maybe it's about time you accepted it.

00:20:36.210 --> 00:20:37.550
Accepted it?

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:41.420
I had a thought
when I looked at you my first day at school.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:45.850
I could tell that you thought
having a back-seat role suited you,

00:20:45.850 --> 00:20:49.640
that you put yourself down
and turned away from what's important.

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:53.600
Like the feelings of people around you,
and people who care for you.

00:20:55.230 --> 00:20:56.900
That's why I made up my mind.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:20:59.070
You need to accept
you're no second banana, Joro,

00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:03.530
but the glue
that holds them all together.

00:21:03.530 --> 00:21:06.320
I thought that's how I'll pay you back.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:09.200
Is that what you were always...

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:12.290
Joro, everyone loves you.

00:21:12.960 --> 00:21:15.500
They're together because of you.

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:18.750
Are you able to accept that feeling?

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:23.550
Yeah. I will accept it.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:24.470
After all...

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:29.510
<i>I'm surrounded by cute girls
and a best friend I can count on.</i>

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:33.430
<i>I can't just be a background character
if I hang out with an awesome bunch like them.</i>

00:21:33.430 --> 00:21:37.900
<i>In fact, maybe there is
no such thing as a background character.</i>

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:41.900
I'm an average,
run-of-the-mill main character.

00:21:43.860 --> 00:21:45.110
Bullseye, I guess.

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:49.330
Whatever the problem, I'll solve it!

00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:52.370
<i>Is what I thought at that moment, but...</i>

00:21:56.250 --> 00:22:01.460
Please help me get Sanshokuin and Oga
to be girlfriend-boyfriend!

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:04.970
I can't handle this problem!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.980
SPECIAL EPISODE
I POLITELY MOVE THINGS FORWARD
